WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:09.278
The journey starts with a department purchase request. Add the required items,
quantities, specifications, and target date.

00:00:09.728 --> 00:00:17.896
Send the request for review. The sourcing officer can approve it, ask for
changes, or reject it with a reason.

00:00:18.996 --> 00:00:26.684
The sourcing officer turns an approved request into a tender, with clear
requirements, terms, and a submission deadline.

00:00:27.134 --> 00:00:32.817
The published tender provides the shared requirements that suppliers use to
prepare their offers.

00:00:33.917 --> 00:00:42.790
Eligible, approved suppliers receive invitations. Each supplier reviews the
tender and accepts or declines the invitation.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:53.497
Accepted suppliers prepare their offers with item prices, tax, extra costs,
delivery terms, and supporting documents, then submit before the deadline.

00:00:54.597 --> 00:01:01.460
The sourcing officer reviews offer details and confirms compliance before
sending eligible offers to the committee.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:11.318
The four committee members agree financial and technical weights, then score
each eligible offer. Their combined results support the recommendation.

00:01:12.418 --> 00:01:20.835
The committee prepares its report. The sourcing officer reviews it and can
approve it, request changes, or reject it.

00:01:21.285 --> 00:01:29.508
The sourcing manager reviews the approved report and nominated offer, then
refers the proposal to the CEO and Chiefs for their decision.

00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:38.386
The CEO and Chiefs review the nominated offer and record their decisions.
Approval allows the tender to be awarded.

00:01:38.836 --> 00:01:50.884
Tiryaq records the outcome, closes the tender, and notifies the relevant
parties. Requests, offers, evaluations, and approvals remain connected.
